  "answer": "**Final status: passing.** On the second verification run (`20261021T111206Z-873876`), build, unit and component tests all passed. It took one fix.\n\n**What failed:** On the first run, the unit tests failed with exit code 2. The only failing test was `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`, and it failed on both net9.0 and net10.0. Component tests were skipped because the run stopped after the unit failure.\n\n**Root cause:** When the actual response has a field that the expected response doesn't, the diff formatter labelled it `<not present>`. The test expects `<absent>`, to pair with the existing `<missing>` label for the opposite case. The label comes from `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`.\n\n**What changed:** One line in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`: `TestColor.Subtle(\"<not present>\")` became `TestColor.Subtle(\"<absent>\")`. The fixer agent left the test alone and found no other uses of the old text.\n\nNothing was committed. Integration tests (`make integration`) are not part of the configured checks, so they weren't run.",
